{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/71072-aliens-in-hunter","id":71072,"title":"Aliens in Hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-12T23:33:27-08:00","id":71072,"title":"Aliens in Hunter","content":"I've been chewing on the tidbits I can glean from the Delta Green fiction anthology that's up on Kickstarter, and it sragged me back to my old idea of incorporating DG into Hunter: the Vigil. The two pair nicely - Delta Green is a textbook Compact, and &quot;keep the populace safe from and ignorant of the Mythos&quot; rather easily becomes &quot;keep the populace safe from and ignorant of the wider supernatural World of Darkness&quot; - but a rather crucial piece of things gets snagged in the transition. Delta Green is hardly the organization that we know and love without their counterparts in MAJESTIC-12, the government-sanctioned group that works alongside the Greys but disbelieve any further paranormal shenanigans. It had me wondering about how to use aliens in nWoD, specifically in a Hunter context.<br /> <br /> The existing stance on aliens seems to largely be &quot;a fair number of them are Fae,&quot; but I want to puzzle out extraterrestrials as a separate force. Do you have any compelling ideas for aliens im the WoD? Should their be aliens beyond the Greys (the Lizardmen and Nordics are likely culprits, alongside some spooky bug-things or fungi from somewhere else)? What sort of material would you want in a dedicated aliens book, a la Night Stalkers and its companions? What would the existing Compacts/Conspiracies think of aliens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-13-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T21:03:07-08:00","id":71809,"title":"","content":"I believe Infinite Macabre, the Mirrors book, has mechanics for making aliens. Reptiloids and greys, at least.<br /> I suppose if you wanted more than one kind of alien out there you'd have to figure out why there's different species of aliens on Earth (are they invading in tandem? do they have different motives?). Or at least how did they get there? And what are they doing now that they're here (because if they're not doing anything, why would hunters even notice them to go after them?).<br /> The Hunter books tend to follow the formula, 'instances of (splat) in the past from the eyes of hunters' with some plot hooks, then how the major compacts and conspiracies deal with them, then 2 or 3 compacts and a conspiracy, with some new hunter mechanics (some for the conspiracy, usually 1 splat-related endowment for the other conspiracies), some dread powers and a section on how to involve the splat in your games, then samples from Philadelphia.<br /> <br /> I think a good way to handle it would be to let some of the aliens be things fans could link to existing splats (That's a cryptid, that's an abyssal spirit) but also things that simply couldn't be explained with an understanding of another book (what the hell is that? Aliens!?). I think the conspiracies and compacts would be pretty easy, possibly the conspiracy as a tech-based group, one compact about a ufo-watch, another possibly having sold out to aliens and thus keep an eye out for not-their-buddy aliens to kill.<br /> <br /> Thanks for informing me about the Delta Green KS, by the way, I agree that a MAJESTIC-12 setup would be intriguing in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:00:56-08:00","id":71885,"title":"","content":"There are Grey Aliens in Summoners. Though they're very odd and don't seem to work right, they have hyper advanced tech but it's really more like a magical ability; not unlike the Greys from DG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}